# s3_key_stream: first step of the paid phase
#
# phase      at s2's peak (56,283,336 kB) every named object besides the slurp is <= 75.5 MB (0.13%),
#            each below the 962.9 MB anon:[heap]; free fixes s1, s2 taken (README.md: paid when no free
#            fix remains).
# object     heap:comm.hpp:266:shark::Dealer::Dealer 56,416.3 MB (97.9%): one `new char[size]` in the
#            oneShot branch holding the whole preprocessing file (56,416,290,832 B on party 0 = server.dat).
# lever      reload via Dealer(filename, oneShot = false) -> FileBuf; reads strictly sequential;
#            isMem() never called. Image carries an 8 MiB stream read buffer.
# cost       from baseline: +26.9% (8 KiB stock buffer), +6.4% (8 MiB), +8.5% (64 MiB). 8 MiB removes
#            99.9% of syscalls and recovers 20.5 of 26.9 points; fewer syscalls beyond that is worse:
#            residual not syscall-bound (off-path.md, off-path-runs/).
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: shark::Dealer::Dealer
OMP_NUM_THREADS=4
